1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
You're taking Clomid,
but still no pregnancy.

2
00:00:03,247 --> 00:00:07,020
And suddenly it's a
full-blown household crisis:

3
00:00:07,088 --> 00:00:09,770
"Do we start a new box,
or do we change doctors?"

4
00:00:10,269 --> 00:00:12,810
Before you sprint to
the late-night pharmacy,

5
00:00:12,902 --> 00:00:15,460
there's one question to answer first:

6
00:00:15,478 --> 00:00:19,790
did this treatment actually
trigger ovulation, yes or no?

7
00:00:19,886 --> 00:00:21,710
Because not ovulating at all,

8
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:24,730
and ovulating perfectly
without getting pregnant,

9
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:27,490
are two completely different stories.

10
00:00:27,648 --> 00:00:30,550
It's the difference between
"the car won't even start"

11
00:00:31,048 --> 00:00:32,930
and "the engine runs beautifully,

12
00:00:32,930 --> 00:00:36,140
but somebody forgot to
release the parking brake."

13
00:00:36,428 --> 00:00:38,240
I'm Dr. Senai Aksoy.

14
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:41,320
Today we'll look at why this
medication has its limits,

15
00:00:41,699 --> 00:00:46,500
and when you need to be able to say:
"Okay, folks, this tactic isn't working.

16
00:00:46,542 --> 00:00:48,030
We're changing the plan."

17
00:00:48,296 --> 00:00:51,850
Picture the kitchen table: the
salt shaker, the box of pills,

18
00:00:52,274 --> 00:00:55,270
and that famous magnetic
calendar on the fridge.

19
00:00:55,314 --> 00:00:58,120
The days are ticked off
in neon highlighter;

20
00:00:58,138 --> 00:01:01,340
it looks like NASA's countdown
for a launch to Mars.

21
00:01:01,414 --> 00:01:04,610
Romance? Zero. It's a military operation.

22
00:01:05,151 --> 00:01:10,180
And the little inner voice kicks in:
"It didn't work last month. It's fate...

23
00:01:10,297 --> 00:01:12,600
Fine, I'll start another box."

24
00:01:12,751 --> 00:01:15,750
So, we congratulate the
calendar on its discipline.

25
00:01:16,171 --> 00:01:20,610
But it has one small flaw: it
can't read a hormone panel!

26
00:01:20,639 --> 00:01:25,200
If we listen to it, we'll carry on
like this until the 2028 Olympics.

27
00:01:25,329 --> 00:01:28,190
The active ingredient, clomiphene citrate,

28
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:30,790
actually plays a little
trick on the brain.

29
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:34,310
It scrambles the estrogen
sensors, and the brain thinks:

30
00:01:34,355 --> 00:01:36,710
"Oh no, there's no estrogen down there.

31
00:01:36,828 --> 00:01:38,670
Has the shop closed or what?!"

32
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:41,060
So it raises FSH.

33
00:01:41,164 --> 00:01:43,750
That's the hormone that
makes the follicle grow,

34
00:01:43,821 --> 00:01:47,760
that little pocket that holds the
egg, all the way to ovulation.

35
00:01:47,842 --> 00:01:53,260
But let's bust a myth right away: a
bigger follicle doesn't mean a better egg.

36
00:01:53,702 --> 00:01:58,220
Put a completely blurry passport
photo in a huge gilded frame,

37
00:01:58,293 --> 00:02:02,800
like a painting in the Louvre, and
the photo doesn't suddenly turn 4K.

38
00:02:02,853 --> 00:02:06,360
Nothing shows that clomiphene
improves egg quality.

39
00:02:06,427 --> 00:02:10,950
It just bangs on the door, shouting:
"Come on, somebody has to come out!"

40
00:02:11,116 --> 00:02:15,380
First scenario: you took the
pills, but zero ovulation.

41
00:02:15,659 --> 00:02:20,240
Instead of opening another box, you need
to find out who's on strike in there.

42
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:23,340
Polycystic ovary syndrome, PCOS?

43
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:27,500
The thyroid or prolactin, playing
a solo outside the orchestra?

44
00:02:27,654 --> 00:02:30,920
Or maybe, on the "get bikini-ready" diet,

45
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:34,640
one lettuce leaf a day and
three hours of intense exercise,

46
00:02:34,674 --> 00:02:36,720
the brain said: "Famine alert!

47
00:02:36,771 --> 00:02:40,670
Cut the breaker on the reproductive
system, we're saving our own skin!"?

48
00:02:40,939 --> 00:02:43,280
Each cause has its own treatment.

49
00:02:43,350 --> 00:02:48,460
If the missing ovulation is linked to
PCOS, with no other fertility factor,

50
00:02:48,484 --> 00:02:53,140
the 2023 international guidelines
place letrozole first-line.

51
00:02:53,235 --> 00:02:57,650
That doesn't mean Clomid is retired:
the choice depends on the diagnosis,

52
00:02:57,659 --> 00:03:00,780
your previous response, and your
country's prescribing rules.

53
00:03:01,233 --> 00:03:05,900
And please, no self-medicating on
advice from the tea-and-gossip crowd:

54
00:03:05,953 --> 00:03:10,350
"My sister-in-law took it and had
triplets, so take two pills, sweetheart!"

55
00:03:10,499 --> 00:03:15,690
Second scenario: ovulation clearly
happened, but still no pregnancy.

56
00:03:15,912 --> 00:03:19,780
Here, the medication tells you:
"I got the egg to the exit door.

57
00:03:19,809 --> 00:03:23,200
What happens next isn't my
department." And it's right!

58
00:03:23,246 --> 00:03:25,790
Ovulation is just the movie trailer.

59
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:29,520
Clomid is not a plumber, it
won't unblock a blocked tube!

60
00:03:29,611 --> 00:03:32,140
And when she takes the
treatment, his sperm,

61
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:34,680
lounging on the couch
watching the game highlights,

62
00:03:34,719 --> 00:03:37,080
don't suddenly turn into Michael Phelps.

63
00:03:37,135 --> 00:03:40,860
No, medicine hasn't received
that Bluetooth update yet!

64
00:03:40,888 --> 00:03:46,030
The workup involves the couple, and age
and good timing matter just as much.

65
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:49,220
And by the way, take women
who already ovulate like

66
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:53,000
Swiss clockwork but have
unexplained infertility.

67
00:03:53,070 --> 00:03:57,620
Giving them clomiphene alone, with a
cheerful "Set an alarm on your phone,

68
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,640
tonight we're working overtime,"

69
00:03:59,764 --> 00:04:03,030
hasn't been shown to improve
the chances of pregnancy.

70
00:04:03,287 --> 00:04:05,260
When the factory is already running,

71
00:04:05,303 --> 00:04:08,510
there's no point shaking the
manager every five minutes.

72
00:04:08,572 --> 00:04:11,720
Stimulating the ovaries for
an insemination, though?

73
00:04:11,828 --> 00:04:13,470
That's a different story.

74
00:04:13,756 --> 00:04:16,340
So, how many months do we keep trying?

75
00:04:16,742 --> 00:04:21,650
The French prescribing information
sets a maximum of six treatment cycles.

76
00:04:21,670 --> 00:04:26,440
But careful: that number six isn't
a loyalty card, "buy five coffees,

77
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:30,760
get the sixth free," that you absolutely
have to get stamped to the end.

78
00:04:30,817 --> 00:04:34,960
If three courses at the recommended
dose haven't produced ovulation,

79
00:04:35,005 --> 00:04:37,260
the trial is considered over.

80
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:41,800
And if ovulation happens but there's
still no pregnancy after several tries,

81
00:04:41,974 --> 00:04:45,830
we review the workup and the
strategy, sometimes sooner.

82
00:04:45,918 --> 00:04:50,080
Injections, insemination
or IVF aren't levels in a

83
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:53,700
video game that you have to
clear one by one, in order.

84
00:04:53,761 --> 00:04:56,470
We take the route that fits your couple.

85
00:04:56,678 --> 00:04:58,460
And a sentence I hear a lot:

86
00:04:58,537 --> 00:05:01,860
"I had three pills left at the
bottom of last month's box.

87
00:05:01,969 --> 00:05:04,380
It seemed a shame to waste
them, so I took them."

88
00:05:04,769 --> 00:05:08,520
Come on, it's not half a lemon
forgotten in the fridge door!

89
00:05:08,534 --> 00:05:12,390
Having pills lying around
is not a medical indication.

90
00:05:12,568 --> 00:05:14,450
Proper monitoring means ultrasound,

91
00:05:15,017 --> 00:05:17,590
to watch the follicles and
the lining of the uterus,

92
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:20,890
and hormone tests can
help assess ovulation.

93
00:05:21,059 --> 00:05:24,290
Because clomiphene has a
peculiar sense of humor.

94
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:28,470
By blocking estrogen receptors,
it can thin the uterine lining,

95
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:31,950
the endometrium, right where
the baby needs to settle in.

96
00:05:31,997 --> 00:05:36,070
It's like insisting to your guests,
"No, really, stay the night!"

97
00:05:36,165 --> 00:05:38,690
and while they're taking off
their shoes in the hallway,

98
00:05:38,729 --> 00:05:40,370
you sell all the beds.

99
00:05:40,476 --> 00:05:44,110
Or the other way around: several
follicles take off at the same time,

100
00:05:44,468 --> 00:05:47,380
and hello, risk of multiple pregnancy.

101
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:50,690
Now, two minutes without
jokes, for safety.

102
00:05:50,876 --> 00:05:56,590
Hot flashes, headaches or mild abdominal
discomfort are possible side effects.

103
00:05:56,646 --> 00:06:00,970
But blurred vision, flashes of
light, spots in front of your eyes,

104
00:06:01,466 --> 00:06:04,450
or any other unusual visual disturbance...

105
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:07,770
never tell yourself, "It's
just low blood pressure."

106
00:06:07,829 --> 00:06:11,310
Stop the treatment and
contact your doctor promptly.

107
00:06:11,349 --> 00:06:13,150
A full eye exam is needed.

108
00:06:13,612 --> 00:06:16,000
If nothing else explains these symptoms,

109
00:06:16,066 --> 00:06:18,890
clomiphene must be stopped permanently.

110
00:06:18,890 --> 00:06:21,020
Don't restart it on your own.

111
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:25,150
Same goes for severe abdominal
pain, rapid swelling of the belly,

112
00:06:25,489 --> 00:06:29,270
or shortness of breath:
that's a medical emergency.

113
00:06:29,297 --> 00:06:30,910
Don't wait for your next appointment.

114
00:06:31,467 --> 00:06:34,450
And of course, before
every new treatment cycle,

115
00:06:34,467 --> 00:06:37,580
we check that a pregnancy
hasn't already started.

116
00:06:37,752 --> 00:06:40,920
If it didn't work with
Clomid, it's not your fault.

117
00:06:40,965 --> 00:06:45,050
At your next appointment, simply ask
your doctor these three questions:

118
00:06:45,050 --> 00:06:47,320
"Have I really ovulated?"

119
00:06:47,578 --> 00:06:49,670
"What other factors have we checked?"

120
00:06:49,790 --> 00:06:52,350
"At what point do we move to plan B?"

121
00:06:52,534 --> 00:06:54,360
It's not the calendar on the fridge that

122
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,620
should decide whether to open a new box,

123
00:06:56,721 --> 00:06:59,490
but the answers to those three questions.

124
00:06:59,551 --> 00:07:02,580
This information doesn't
replace a medical consultation.

125
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:05,980
The medication, the dose
and the length of treatment

126
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:08,930
are decided with the
doctor who follows you.

127
00:07:09,029 --> 00:07:10,510
Alright, ciao!
